Z||000002||btoth||06-10-2001||02:11 PM||||If you can still see the coolent in the overflow tank you can just fill it from there.  Otherwise, for filling the system, you pour into the back until the coolent come up to the top in the front and then cap the front and fill the rest of the way in the back.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrgone||06-10-2001||02:52 PM||||great, that all i needed to know<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-10-2001||08:31 PM||||As stated in my article... purging the heater should only be needed after heater repair or the system is drained and let air into the heater lines.||||reg||1
